mlrv-pd — Pure Data port of mlrv2
==================================

This directory is a from-scratch Pure Data reimplementation of the
behavior found in ../mlrv2 (Max/MSP patches), which is itself an
unmodified fork of:

    https://github.com/trentgill/mlrv2

...a refactoring of Brian Crabtree's original "mlr", extended by
Trent Gill (galapagoose) and Michael Felix (%).

License status of the original
-------------------------------
Neither this fork (oth-body/mlrv--) nor upstream (trentgill/mlrv2)
carries a LICENSE file. Absent one, the original Max/MSP source is
all-rights-reserved by default. No file, patch, or byte from
../mlrv2/patchers/*.maxpat has been copied into this directory —
everything here is written from scratch against the *observed
behavior and wire protocols* of the original (grid/OSC layout,
signal-flow shape, parameter ranges visible in comments), which is
not itself copyrightable.

Do not add a LICENSE file to this directory implying original
authors' work is being relicensed. If mlrv-pd is ever distributed
beyond personal use, get explicit permission from Trent Gill /
Michael Felix first, since the intent (feature parity with their
design) is close enough to derivative work that it deserves asking,
license technicality aside.

Known gaps vs. the original (see handoff doc for detail)
----------------------------------------------------------
- The original's `metapattern.maxpat` / `gridcell.maxpat` use
  `xrecord~` / `xgroove~`, objects from Thomas Grill's third-party
  "xsample" external, not stock Max. `mixer.maxpat` itself contains
  the in-patch comment "xsample external not found" — i.e. the
  original may not run cleanly in a current Max install either.
  This port does not attempt to replicate xsample-specific behavior;
  it targets what `groove~`/`play~`-based patchers do.
